      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah only allocations whose size is known at compile time can be on the stack.\n\nThis works, but what\u0027s wrong with just stripping out empty strings from the beginning/end of the slice? The only benefit of the stack based array is that you can strip out empty strings from the middle of 2 nonempty strings. But if there are empty strings in the middle, that means `filepath.Join` will already have to do a new allocation, and thus the empty string in the middle is not really a problem.",
